# --- build output ------------------------------------------------------------
bin/
obj/
dist/
# The Windows libraries package.sh fetches to cross-build with.
deps/
*.o
*.exe
*.x86_64
DreamQuest.x86_64
.claude/

# --- art ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# assets/ is the game's own art -- modelled, rendered and drawn by the tools in
# tools/ -- so it travels with the repository and a fresh clone runs as it
# stands. docs/ASSETS.md records what makes what.
#
# Four things under it are not ours to pass on, or are build scratch:
#   _raw            unpacked copies of whatever packs were downloaded
#   _render         Blender's full-size renders, rebuilt on demand
#   _cut_buildings  tilecut scratch output
#   fonts           a system font copied locally; the game falls back to one
#   icons/armour    the optional CraftPix equipment icon packs
# A trailing comment on a pattern line is part of the pattern, not a comment,
# which is why these are listed above rather than beside.
assets/_raw/
assets/_render/
assets/_cut_buildings/
assets/fonts/
assets/icons/armour/

# Both written by the importer from the optional equipment icon packs, so
# data/items.json never refers to art that may not be installed. Generated
# rather than authored, and meaningless without the packs, so neither is
# committed.
data/items_armour.json
data/loot_tables_armour.json

# --- local state -------------------------------------------------------------
saves/
settings.json
imgui.ini

# --- editors and OS ----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
__pycache__/

# --- saves -------------------------------------------------------------------
# The backup the game keeps beside each slot, the half-written file a save goes
# through on its way, and what a deleted slot is put aside as. None of them is
# a save anybody made on purpose.
saves/*.bak
saves/*.tmp
saves/*.deleted
